{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. My recent trip lived up to every expectation and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Shibuya Crossing was a must-see – a perfectly orchestrated chaos of people. I spent hours exploring quirky shops in Harajuku and marveling at the vibrant street art in Shinjuku. The food scene? Unbelievable. From Michelin-starred restaurants to tiny ramen shops tucked away in alleys, every meal was an adventure.\n\nNext up was Kyoto, a stark contrast to Tokyo’s modernity. Here, I wandered through bamboo forests, visited breathtaking temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion), and felt transported back in time.  The traditional tea ceremonies were incredibly peaceful and insightful. \n\nOne of the highlights was simply getting lost in the smaller streets, discovering hidden gardens and charming cafes.  The kindness and politeness of the Japanese people were truly remarkable. \n\nJapan is a country of contrasts – ancient traditions seamlessly blending with cutting-edge technology. It’s a place that challenges your perceptions and leaves you wanting more.  I’m already dreaming of my return!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1426810771226883}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11408442258834839}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.25964632630348206}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.6041982769966125}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.010067163035273552}, {"token": "▁The", "logprob": -0.056274723